For every sufficiently small fixed $\upsilon>0$, the parameters may be chosen so that some $ho<L^{-2+\upsilon}$ satisfies  egin{equation} u_j+|\lambda_j| \le C_H(1+K)^Cho^{K-j}, \qquad 0\le j\le K, \end{equation} uniformly in $N\ge K$. After the respective bulk scalars have been removed, write the endpoint densities as $e^{X_i(q)}\Xi_i(q)$. On every common admitted terminal torus of volume $v$,  egin{align} 
orm{X_1-X_2}_\infty&\le D_Hv\delta_K,
onumber\ \sup_x\sum_{\lambda:x\in P_\lambda} e^{As_\lambda}
orm{k_{1,\lambda}-k_{2,\lambda}}_\infty &\le D_H\delta_K, \qquad \delta_K=L^{-(2-\upsilon)K}. \end{align} The constants are independent of depths and periods. The two mirrored inclined trajectories at depth $N$ have the same endpoint estimates with $K=N$, when their output lists are expressed in common coordinates.
